==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Rain which is unusually [[acidic]] ([[pH]] of less than the natural range of 5 to 6); caused mainly by [[atmospheric]] [[pollution]] with [[sulphur dioxide]] and [[nitrogen]] [[compound]]s.
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Airborne Pollutants|work=The New York Times|date=1987-01-20|url=https://www.nytimes.com/1987/01/20/science/science-watch-airborne-pollutants.html|issn=0362-4331|passage='''Acid rain''' forms when water in the atmosphere condenses on particles containing acid-forming pollutants, such as sulfate produced by the burning of fossil fuels and nitrogen oxides from automobile exhausts.}}

